## Forbidden in New Code

- `domain/port/` packages or `*Port` interface suffix — prefer `*Repository` / `*Gateway`
- Hexagonal `adapter/in` / `adapter/out` package names — use `presentation` / `infrastructure`
- Browser / mobile direct calls to Python services or explore-ai

**Legacy note:** existing `*ApiAdapter` classes under `infrastructure/adapters` may remain; new domain-facing interfaces still live in `domain/` as Repository/Gateway.

## Domain Rules

- No framework annotations in domain
- Prefer rich models (behavior on entities); avoid anemic getters-only types
- Repository/Gateway: interface in domain, implementation in infrastructure
- Names align with [Glossary](../../docs/Glossary.md) Preferred Terms

## UI & Client Stack (always)

- Visual language: **Instagram-consistent** and **Apple HIG-consistent**
- Styling: **Emotion** (`@emotion/styled` / project emotion helpers)
- State optimisation: **Redux Toolkit** where client state applies
- Utilities: prefer **lodash** for collection/object helpers when it clarifies code

## TypeScript Naming

| Type | Rule | Example |
|------|------|---------|
| Domain model | PascalCase | `Post`, `FeedEntry` |
| Value object | PascalCase | `PostId` |
| Repository | PascalCase + Repository | `FeedRepository` |
| Use case / service | PascalCase + descriptive | `ExploreService`, `GetFeedUseCase` |
| Controller | PascalCase + Controller | `PostController` |
| Adapter (infra) | PascalCase + Adapter | `FeedApiAdapter` |
| Methods | camelCase | `getExplore` |
| Constants | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE | `MAX_PAGE_SIZE` |

## REST / API

- Nest routes under `/api/v1/...`
- Controllers stay thin; business rules in application/domain
- Explore AI upstream goes through Nest BFF (`/ai/explore/*`), not the client

## Test Naming

```
should_expectedResult_when_condition
```

Pyramid: Unit ~70% / Integration ~20% / E2E ~10%.  
Details: [developer skill → testing](../skills/developer/references/testing.md)

## Checklist

- [ ] Domain has no outward dependencies
- [ ] No circular dependencies
- [ ] Entities encapsulate behavior
- [ ] Clients call only NestJS (`/api/v1`)

